  "question": {
    "text": "A black body at a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>227</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi>C</mi></math> radiates heat at the rate of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cal</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. At a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>727</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> the rate of heat radiated per unit area in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cal</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is",
